      "title": "Saudi Arabia strategy challenged by anti-Houthi forces in Yemen",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/16/saudi-arabia-challenged-yemeni-allies-ceding-ground-houthis",
      "description": "<p>Accusations of incompetence follow retreat of Riyadh-backed forces in effort to relieve siege of Taiz and protect Aden </p><p>Saudi Arabia has been accused by anti-Houthi forces over its military strategy after its Yemeni allies withdrew troops from the strategic Bab al-Mandab strait and pulled back forces from parts of Marib in the central part of the country.</p><p>The Saudi-backed government explained the repositioning by saying the strategic priority was to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/30/houthis-taiz-stone-age-yemen-city-siege\">break the attritional siege on Taiz</a>, Yemen’s third city, and to protect Aden, the southern port city in which the Saudi-backed and UN-recognised government is now based.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/16/saudi-arabia-challenged-yemeni-allies-ceding-ground-houthis\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
